This reminds me of a funny experience in Nethack that I had:

Around level 28ish, somewhere in Gehnnom, and I had 
disintigration-resistance (ate a black dragon corpse), magic-resistance 
(GSDM), reflection (SoR), so on and so forth... and had like 4 blessed 
luckstones.  Anyway, I offered a corpse on an alter to my god, Crom (I am 
playing a barbarian), and I glimpsed a four-leaf clover at my feet (not 
unusual).  Anyway, I figured I might as well pray and see if I get any 
items... (I already have a +7 blessed rustproofed Vorpal Blade, so I 
really couldn't care if I didn't get it or not...).  Well, in Gehnnom, 
Crom couldn't help me.  I instead prayed to Moloch.  OOPS.  Anyway, he 
decides to send a lightning bolt to fry me (I was scared to hit enter... 
urrk!) but my SoR bounced it.  I got the "I am not happy!" type message 
from Moloch, and then a ray of disintigration tried to zap me.  Well, it 
said "you bask in the black glow" or something like that, then the "I 
cannot believe this!" message came up, and then I was free to trek along 
my merry way.

Normally, this would have killed me out of the hat, but I just sat back 
and laughed my ass off when I saw this.  First time a I wasn't killed 'by 
a pissed-off deity'.  =)

